power: supply: add POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGING_ENABLED

The enum value the PM8150B charger driver (and the downstream Qualcomm
vendor drivers it follows) use to expose and control the charging
enable bit. The pmOS soc/qualcomm-sm8250 tree carries the same value;
mainline does not, so the driver fails to build against pristine
7.2.8. Deliberately no sysfs name: the driver only uses it internally
and the pmOS tree does not expose it either.

Source: darknagel/oneplus-instantnoodlep-nura-unofficial against the
pmOS soc tree (sm8250-7.2.0_git20261010).
--- a/include/linux/power_supply.h
+++ b/include/linux/power_supply.h
@@ -178,6 +178,7 @@
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_MANUFACTURE_DAY,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_INTERNAL_RESISTANCE,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATE_OF_HEALTH,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGING_ENABLED,
 	/* Properties of type `const char *' */
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_MODEL_NAME,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_MANUFACTURER,
